#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# add_column

#% text
# `add_column(ds, c, f)` gives the dataset `ds` with column `c` set to `f(row)` for each row.

#% text
# `add_column(ds, c, values)` gives `ds` with column `c` set to the list `values`, one per row.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A column `c` that `ds` already has is replaced where it is; a new one comes last.

#% item
# The calls `f(row)` are evaluated like the elements of `map`; a failure among them is the result.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
shop = dataset([["item", "kind", "price", "stock"], ["pen", "office", 1.5, 40], ["lamp", "home", 24.0, 3], ["ink", "office", 6.0, missing()], ["mug", "home", 8.5, 12]])
add_column(shop, "cents", r => round(100 * r["price"]))
#% output
#= item | kind   | price |   stock | cents
#= -----+--------+-------+---------+------
#= pen  | office |   1.5 |      40 |   150
#= lamp | home   |  24.0 |       3 |  2400
#= ink  | office |   6.0 | missing |   600
#= mug  | home   |   8.5 |      12 |   850
#= dataset: 4 rows, 5 columns

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A list of values:

#% cell
add_column(shop, "rank", [3, 1, 4, 2])
#% output
#= item | kind   | price |   stock | rank
#= -----+--------+-------+---------+-----
#= pen  | office |   1.5 |      40 |    3
#= lamp | home   |  24.0 |       3 |    1
#= ink  | office |   6.0 | missing |    4
#= mug  | home   |   8.5 |      12 |    2
#= dataset: 4 rows, 5 columns

#% text
# Replacing a column:

#% cell
add_column(shop, "price", r => 2 * r["price"])
#% output
#= item | kind   | price |   stock
#= -----+--------+-------+--------
#= pen  | office |   3.0 |      40
#= lamp | home   |  48.0 |       3
#= ink  | office |  12.0 | missing
#= mug  | home   |  17.0 |      12
#= dataset: 4 rows, 4 columns

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A list must have one value per row:

#% cell
add_column(shop, "rank", [1, 2])
#% output
#! failure(shape_mismatch, add_column)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `dataset`, `column`, `aggregate`
